  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 5, 2026.</p>

  <p>
    Social Agent is private operational software used by Shariq Hirani for
    publishing and growth reporting for his engineering site and Oris. These
    terms describe the narrow conditions under which an authorized person may
    use it. They are provided for review and information and are not presented
    as a substitute for legal advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Permission to access</h2>

  <p>
    You may access Social Agent only when the operator has explicitly authorized
    you. Do not share login details, OAuth grants, tokens, or other credentials.
    Do not attempt to reach the private dashboard, data, or provider connections
    without permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Authorized data and accounts</h2>

  <p>
    Connect or use third-party accounts and data only when you have authority to
    do so. Google access is limited to the read-only permissions described in
    the <a href="/social-agent/privacy/">privacy notice</a>. Third-party
    providers keep their own terms, access controls, definitions, quotas, and
    availability rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Publishing remains human-controlled</h2>

  <p>
    Notion is the curation and approval surface. A publication requires a human <strong
      >Approved</strong
    > decision and a due
    <strong>Post at</strong> time. Growth data and reports cannot approve, schedule,
    rewrite, or publish content on their own.
  </p>

  <h2>Reporting limits</h2>

  <p>
    Reports reflect the data, definitions, time periods, and coverage supplied
    by each provider. Some results are partial, delayed, unavailable, or subject
    to provider limits. A missing observation is not necessarily zero. Reports
    are advisory and do not guarantee traffic, search position, audience growth,
    marketing performance, or any other outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and changes</h2>

  <p>
    Social Agent is maintained as private tooling. Features, integrations, and
    reporting may change, pause, or become unavailable. No public uptime,
    support-response, compatibility, or service-level guarantee is offered.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>

  <p>
    For questions about authorized access, these terms, or data handling, use
    the <a href="/about#contact">contact options on the About page</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    The <a href="/social-agent/">Social Agent overview</a> describes the tool's purpose
    and intended private audience.
  </p>
</SocialAgentPage>
